window.docContents[220].resolve({"/Environment/#envOverview___safetyErrors":{"contents":"\n\nUsing a cvc.lean type after its manager has been freed is rejected due to the quantification of the\nΩ instance. While this guarantees no use-after-free, the error message is a regular lean\ntype-error and its meaning is pretty obscure.\n\ndef mkSort : Env Srt := Srt.int\n\n#eval do\n  let sortWithDeadTermManager ← Env.runIO mkSort\n  println! \"dangling pointer: {sortWithDeadTermManager}\"\n\n\nType mismatch\n  mkSort\nhas type\n  Env Srt\nbut is expected to have type\n  Env ?m.6\n\nNote: The following definitions were not unfolded because their definition is not exposed:\n  Srt ↦ 2\n\n\n","context":"Cvc.lean -- High-Level CVC5 API\u0009Environment\u0009Environment","header":"2.2.1. Ω  and  Env  safety errors","id":"/Environment/#envOverview___safetyErrors"}});